b at their head were congenial, and being akin to their own race, had a warm welcome (Gen. 47:5, 6).","verses":63,"father":"","mother":"","v":[4,6,7]},{"id":"canaan_914","name":"Canaan","also":"Canaanites, Canaanite","summary":"The fourth son of Ham (Gen. 10:6). His descendants were under a curse in consequence of the transgression of his father (9:22-27). His eldest son, Zidon, was the father of the Sidonians and Phoenicians.","verses":84,"father":"Ham","mother":"","v":[5,13]},{"id":"abraham_58","name":"Abraham","also":"Abram","summary":"Father of a multitude, son of Terah, named (Gen. 11:27) before his older brothers Nahor and Haran, because he was the heir of the promises. Till the age of seventy, Abram sojourned among his kindred in his native country of Chaldea.","verses":277,"father":"Terah","mother":"","v":[13,24]},{"id":"ephron_1208","name":"Ephron","also":"","summary":"The son of Zohar a Hittite, the owner of the field and cave of Machpelah, which Abraham bought for 400 shekels of silver (Gen. 23:8-17; 25:9; 49:29, 30).","verses":10,"father":"Zohar","mother":"","v":[13]},{"id":"ephraim_1206","name":"Ephraim","also":"","summary":"Double fruitfulness (“for God had made him fruitful in the land of his affliction”). The second son of Joseph, born in Egypt (Gen. 41:52; 46:20).","verses":160,"father":"Joseph","mother":"Asenath","v":[23]},{"id":"manasseh_1928","name":"Manasseh","also":"Manasses","summary":"The elder of the two sons of Joseph. He and his brother Ephraim were afterwards adopted by Jacob as his own sons (48:1).","verses":109,"father":"Joseph","mother":"Asenath","v":[23]},{"id":"machir_1877","name":"Machir","also":"Machirites","summary":"Manasseh’s oldest son (Josh. 17:1), or probably his only son (see 1 Chr. 7:14, 15; comp. Num. 26:29-33; Josh. 13:31). His descendants are referred to under the name of Machirites, being the offspring of Gilead (Num. 26:29).","verses":17,"father":"Manasseh","mother":"Concubine the Aramitess","v":[23]},{"id":"isaac_616","name":"Isaac","also":"","summary":"The only son of Abraham by Sarah. He was the longest lived of the three patriarchs (Gen. 21:1-3).","verses":123,"father":"Abraham","mother":"Sarah","v":[24]}],"places":[{"id":"canaan_272","name":"Canaan","kind":"Region (Country)","lat":31.69353,"lon":34.84388,"summary":"The country which derived its name from the preceding. The name as first used by the Phoenicians denoted only the maritime plain on which Sidon was built.","verses":76,"v":[5,13]},{"id":"egypt_362","name":"Egypt","kind":"Region (Country)","lat":26.4902,"lon":29.8808,"summary":"The land of the Nile and the pyramids, the oldest kingdom of which we have any record, holds a place of great significance in Scripture.","verses":564,"v":[7,11,14,22,26]},{"id":"goshen_490","name":"Goshen","kind":"Region","lat":30.7285,"lon":31.80469,"summary":"A district in Egypt where Jacob and his family settled, and in which they remained till the Exodus (Gen. 45:10; 46:28, 29, 31, etc.). It is called “the land of Goshen” (47:27), and also simply “Goshen” (46:28), and “the land of Rameses” (47:11; Ex. 12:37), for the towns Pithom and Rameses lay within its borders; also Zoan or Tanis (Ps. 78:12).","verses":11,"v":[8]},{"id":"atad_112","name":"Atad","kind":"","lat":null,"lon":null,"summary":"Buckthorn, a place where Joseph and his brethren, when on their way from Egypt to Hebron with the remains of their father Jacob, made for seven days a “great and very sore lamentation.”","verses":2,"v":[10,11]},{"id":"jordan_653","name":"Jordan","kind":"Water (River)","lat":33.18645,"lon":35.61916,"summary":"But besides these two historical fountains there is a third, called the Hasbany, which rises in the bottom of a valley at the western base of Hermon, 12 miles north of Tell-el-Kady.","verses":177,"v":[10,11]},{"id":"abel-mizraim_9","name":"Abel-mizraim","kind":"","lat":null,"lon":null,"summary":"Meadow of Egypt, or mourning of Egypt, a place “beyond,” i.e., on the west of Jordan, at the “threshing-floor of Atad.” Here the Egyptians mourned seventy days for Jacob (Gen. 50:4-11).","verses":1,"v":[11]},{"id":"machpelah_748","name":"Machpelah","kind":"Landmark (Cave)","lat":31.52465,"lon":35.11073,"summary":"Portion; double cave, the cave which Abraham bought, together with the field in which it stood, from Ephron the Hittite, for a family burying-place (Gen. 23).","verses":6,"v":[13]},{"id":"mamre_762","name":"Mamre","kind":"","lat":31.5491,"lon":35.09356,"summary":"The name of the place in the neighbourhood of Hebron where Abraham dwelt (Gen. 23:17, 19; 35:27); called also in Authorized Version (13:18) the “plain of Mamre,” but in Revised Version more correctly “the oaks [marg., ‘terebinths’] of Mamre.”","verses":6,"v":[13]}],"events":[{"id":"death_of_joseph_118","title":"Death of Joseph","year":-1635,"summary":"Passage: Genesis 50:22–26. People: Joseph. Place: Egypt.","v":[22,23,24,25,26]},{"id":"lifetime_of_joseph_103","title":"Lifetime of Joseph","year":-1745,"summary":"Passage: Genesis 30:23–50:22. People: Joseph. Place: Egypt. Lasted about 110 years.","v":[22]}],"traditions":[],"sources":["JFB","MHCC","Wesley"],"tags":{"bsb":[[3130,3130,5307,5921,1,1,6440,1058,5921,5921,5401,5401,0],[3130,3130,6680,7495,7495,5650,5650,5650,2590,2590,1,1,3478,7495,7495,2590,2590],[705,705,705,3117,4390,4390,4390,2590,2590,4713,4713,4713,1058,7657,7657,7657,3117],[3117,3117,3117,1068,1068,5674,5674,3130,1696,413,6547,1004,518,4672,4672,4672,2580,5869,5869,5869,4994,1696,6547,6547],[1,1,7650,7650,7650,7650,7650,559,559,559,595,4191,4191,4191,4191,6912,6912,6912,6912,6913,6913,6913,834,3738,3738,776,776,776,776,776,3667,3667,6258,5927,5927,5927,6912,6912,1,1,7725,7725,7725],[6547,559,5927,5927,6912,6912,1,1,834,7650,7650,7650,7650,7650,7650],[3130,3130,5927,6912,6912,1,1,3605,3605,5650,5650,6547,6547,5927,854,2205,1004,1004,1004,3605,3605,2205,2205,776,776,776,4714,4714],[3605,3605,3605,3130,3130,1004,251,251,251,1,1,1,1004,7535,2945,2945,6629,6629,1241,1241,5800,5800,1657,1